## Overlay model

One chip. Not a toast feed. Not a 100vw strip.

```
type SyncOverlayKind = 'hidden' | 'offline' | 'syncing' | 'error'

type SyncOverlayState =
  | { kind: 'hidden' }
  | { kind: 'offline'; pendingCount: number }
  | { kind: 'syncing'; pendingCount: number }
  | { kind: 'error'; rejectedCount: number }
```

Pure function (unit-test this; do not inline the priority in JSX):

```ts
export function syncOverlayState(input: {
  isOnline: boolean
  pendingCount: number
  rejectedCount: number
}): SyncOverlayState {
  if (!input.isOnline) return { kind: 'offline', pendingCount: input.pendingCount }
  if (input.rejectedCount > 0) return { kind: 'error', rejectedCount: input.rejectedCount }
  if (input.pendingCount > 0) return { kind: 'syncing', pendingCount: input.pendingCount }
  return { kind: 'hidden' }
}
```

**Priority (LOCKED):** offline > error > syncing > hidden.

- Offline still shows when `pendingCount === 0` (user went offline with an empty queue — they must know logging will queue).
- Error is **online + REJECTED > 0**. Do not fold rejected into the spinner.
- CONFLICTED / lock stay on `ConflictReviewCard` / `WorkoutLockBanner`. The chip does not replace them. Both may be visible at once.

### Geometry (LOCKED — sonner viewport, not sonner)

Steal from [sonner](https://github.com/emilkowalski/sonner) `Toaster` viewport (and this repo’s conflict stack):

| Token | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| Positioning | `position: fixed` (never `static` / `relative` / `sticky`). Prefer a portal/`SyncProvider` sibling of `{children}`, same as today’s conflict stack |
| Corner | **`right: 16px; bottom: 16px`** (`right-4 bottom-4`). Side hovering chip, not a top strip |
| Collision | Conflict/lock stack stays `bottom-20` **center**. If both would overlap on a 360px viewport, move **only the queue chip** to `top-4 right-4` while those cards exist. Do not cover the session header’s Complete / Coach–Athlete cluster unless that collision branch is active |
| Flow | `pointer-events: none` on the viewport wrapper; `pointer-events: auto` on the chip if it has Retry |
| Size | Syncing: circle **32×32** (`h-8 w-8`) with spinning lucide `RefreshCw` (already used). Offline / error: compact pill, **max-width 120px** (`SyncQueueBadge` budget), height 32px, `text-[11px] font-mono`. `border-radius` ≤ `--radius-lg` (8px). No nested inner card |
| Surface | `bg-[#131313]` / ink-900, `border border-white/10`. Syncing accent `#007AFF`. Offline `#F5A623`. Error `--ok-red` equivalent (`text-red-500` / `border-red-500/30` as today). No blur, no gradient orb, no `shadow-2xl` on the spinner |
| z-index | `z-40` (below `CenteredDialog` / sidebar / lock cards at `z-50`) |
| Live region | `role="status"` `aria-live="polite"` `aria-atomic="true"` on the chip |
| Idle | **Do not render** the node. `getByTestId('sync-status')` count 0 |

`data-testid="sync-status"` stays on the chip root.

`data-state`:

| kind | `data-state` |
| :--- | :--- |
| hidden | (node absent) |
| offline | `offline` |
| syncing | `syncing` |
| error | `error` |

Copy (keep existing strings unless noted):

| kind | Visible |
| :--- | :--- |
| syncing | Spinner only is OK (user asked for a loading circle). Optional `aria-label="Sync queue {n}"`. Visible count `{n}` may sit in the pill if it still fits 120px |
| offline | `CloudOff` + `Offline — queued locally` (truncate in the pill; full string stays `title` / `aria-label`) |
| error | Exclamation + `Needs review` (or `Rejected {n}`). Optional compact Retry calling existing `triggerSync` for the active workout. **Do not** swallow the error into a spinner |

Do not auto-dismiss offline or error. Syncing unmounts when `pendingCount` hits 0 (no ACK celebration toast).

### What must not move

When the chip mounts or unmounts, these y-positions are invariant (same integer `getBoundingClientRect().top`):

- `[data-testid="app-main"]` first **in-flow** child (the workspace, not the overlay)
- `[data-testid="session-name"]` when a session is open
- The first PLAN/LOG table / `[data-testid="add-lift"]` on the session screen

A test that only checks `sync-status` visibility can still pass with the old bar. The y-assertion is the contract.

